# JSON Request Body for Saving PayPal Payment Method

Based on the documentation, here's the exact structure for the Merchant use case:

```json
{
  "intent": "CAPTURE",
  "payment_source": {
    "paypal": {
      "attributes": {
        "customer": {
          "merchant_customer_id": "[email protected]"
        },
        "vault": {
          "store_in_vault": "ON_SUCCESS",
          "usage_type": "MERCHANT"
        }
      },
      "experience_context": {
        "return_url": "https://example.com/returnUrl",
        "cancel_url": "https://example.com/cancelUrl"
      }
    }
  },
  "purchase_units": [{
    "amount": {
      "currency_code": "USD",
      "value": "100.00"
    }
  }]
}
```

**Key field values shown:**
- `"store_in_vault": "ON_SUCCESS"` - The payment method saves only after successful capture
- `"usage_type": "MERCHANT"` - Indicates merchant-initiated storage (Platform uses `"PLATFORM"`)
- The `merchant_customer_id` is optional for storing your customer identifier

# JSON Request Body for Saving PayPal

Based on the documentation provided, here is the exact JSON structure shown:

```json
{
  "intent": "CAPTURE",
  "payment_source": {
    "paypal": {
      "attributes": {
        "vault": {
          "store_in_vault": "ON_SUCCESS",
          "usage_type": "MERCHANT"
        }
      },
      "experience_context": {
        "return_url": "https://example.com/returnUrl",
        "cancel_url": "https://example.com/cancelUrl"
      }
    }
  },
  "purchase_units": [
    {
      "amount": {
        "currency_code": "USD",
        "value": "100.00"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key findings:**

- The vault object contains only `"store_in_vault"` and `"usage_type"` fields
- **No `customer_type` field appears** in the vault object throughout the documentation
- Enum values shown: `"store_in_vault": "ON_SUCCESS"` and `"usage_type": "MERCHANT"`
- This represents the "single merchant" use case (not platform/marketplace)

